[36m(RolloutManager pid=1913)[0m [2026-09-29 06:15:46.809 rollout_manager] sglang_rollout.py:473 - First rollout sample: ["<|im_start|>user\nJerry’s two daughters play softball on different teams. They each have 8 games this season. Each team practices 4 hours for every game they play. If each game lasts for 2 hours, how many hours will Jerry spend at the field watching his daughters play and practice altogether?\nPut the final numeric answer in \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nLet's break down the problem step by step:\n\n### Given:\n- Jerry’s **two daughters** play **8 games** each.\n- Each **game lasts** 2 hours.\n- **Each team** **practices 4 hours** for each game they play **(i.e., their team's practice time per game is 4 hours)**.\n- The question asks: **How many hours will Jerry spend at the field watching his daughters play?**\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Compute total number of games\n\nJerry has **two daughters**, and each has 8 games:\n\n$$\n2 \\text{ teams} \\times 8 \\text{ games each} = 16 \\text{ games}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Compute total duration of all games\n\nEach game lasts **2 hours**, and we have 16 games:\n\n$$\n16 \\text{ games} \\times 2 \\text{ hours per game} = 32 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Compute total practice time per team\n\nEach team practices 4 hours for each game they play. So, for 8 games:\n\n$$\n8 \\text{ games} \\times 4 \\text{ hours per game} = 32 \\text{ hours per team}\n$$\n\nThere are **two teams**, so total practice time is:\n\n$$\n2 \\text{ teams} \\times 32 \\text{ hours per team} = 64 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Add field watching time and practice time\n\nJerry watches **32 hours** of **field watching**, and **64 hours** of **practice**.\n\n$$\n32 + 64 = \\boxed{96}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{96}\n$$<|im_end|>"], label: 96, reward: 1.0
